#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542228 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abfaf356-6b74-5dfd-8070-e3a60dc372c5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Using Row Totals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16d692bd-0e74-560a-a96c-8d8461608311" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541468} {:answer/id #uuid "74a88296-9ddf-544e-9d53-a64399f2a11a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541663} {:answer/id #uuid "9267e4c1-e2af-5f31-bbf9-2d596a42e1d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541723} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ff7745-61b1-5fe6-ad1b-f5ee14b3580b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541795} {:answer/id #uuid "e265f954-217e-5676-a722-342362e50106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16d692bd-0e74-560a-a96c-8d8461608311" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541468} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebb5d8b0-09a9-5d9e-8e09-86d97b61cdf1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6596362-8154-5a9b-b6ee-af9895a85a60" :question/math-academy-id "q-146227" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=2]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|2}=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=2] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2)]-{\\mu }_{Y|2}^{2} \\\\  & =[{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0+{4}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}]-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =0+0+4-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abfaf356-6b74-5dfd-8070-e3a60dc372c5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Using Row Totals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4abe7f7-40a7-5fee-8c26-2ce6a49da4ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186403} {:answer/id #uuid "02c37c21-5706-5110-839d-3b7f23f1c8c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186404} {:answer/id #uuid "28522e3b-eba5-534c-bcd9-5ef42a50ee9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186405} {:answer/id #uuid "42159274-25fc-5902-8f54-b1273ec708fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186406} {:answer/id #uuid "56837666-e2e8-5a77-9c5c-5bd3b0c1b2ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4abe7f7-40a7-5fee-8c26-2ce6a49da4ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186403} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b741eef-9c5a-588c-9901-de8a736211a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6e8480d-863e-574b-98a7-52fe067fa786" :question/math-academy-id "q-146230" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|1}=\\frac{6}{5}.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{5}{8}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{4}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)]-{\\mu }_{Y|1}^{2} \\\\  & =[{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{5}+{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}]-{(\\frac{6}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{36}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542174 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188328 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92a52324-627c-5796-bc4f-ddeb5380f129" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Using Column Totals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e4f18e3-c2c7-5633-ad51-327c11dda76f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541451} {:answer/id #uuid "1742151a-fdad-55b5-83cf-1eac826f3b6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541470} {:answer/id #uuid "6fb12aa8-c236-5848-bf31-4b538dca5489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541648} {:answer/id #uuid "b235bce1-5f22-5ec4-b929-1a8d2bf6ab80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{40}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541788} {:answer/id #uuid "f97c1141-ae12-5ca0-8969-0f2ba9d5bac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{38}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f97c1141-ae12-5ca0-8969-0f2ba9d5bac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{38}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541945} :answer-field/id #uuid "2224a384-1d96-5035-96d8-8e3991487107" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9a9df102-8e4d-542b-ad62-072cc2469e7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-146287" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{27}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=9$ | $\\frac{5}{27}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=3]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|3}=\\frac{22}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution of $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{27}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=9$ | $\\frac{5}{27}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=9$ | $\\frac{5}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=3] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,3)]-{\\mu }_{X|3}^{2} \\\\  & =[{3}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}+{6}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}+{9}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{9}]-{(\\frac{22}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =1+12+45-\\frac{484}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
